    69	# Phase IL1 — the learner registry, the join check, SWI escapes and a real Popper run
    70	
    71	**Claim.** IL1-C1 to C5 hold on the evidence below, under:
    72	- the owner gate in spec §13 (IL1-D1..D9);
    73	- the IL1-F1 ruling (drop the neutral learner check) and the IL1-F2 ruling
    74	  (accept SWI's LGPL libgmp for local use), both in spec §14;
    75	- amendments IL1-A1 (spec §15) and IL1-A2 (spec §16), each approved by the
    76	  owner on 2026-10-27 before its code changed.
    77	
    78	**The headline.** In invocation 3, a real Popper (v5.0.1, commit 578a4e2)
    79	learned the refunds tutorial's rule from GND's export:
    80	
    81	```prolog
    82	wrong(V0):- f_refund_amount(V0,V1,V2),gt_t_amount__500(V2).
    83	```
    84	
    85	Popper scored it at precision and recall 1.00. SWI over `bk.pl` and GND's
    86	checker over the population both cover the same four examples. `gnd import
    87	ilp-rules` admitted it as one guarded constraint, "amount at most 500"
    88	(induced, proposed, deontic, support 4/4). Getting there took two rendering
    89	amendments, each owner-approved, and three recorded runs.
    90	
    91	## What shipped
    92	
    93	- **`gnd.export.ilp_learners`** (new). One `Learner` entry per `--target`,
    94	  in declaration order: renderer, parser, the run record's learner name, the
    95	  `method` token, the contract, and its own `adapter_version` (IL1-F8).
    96	  `ilp_service` consults it and names no learner. The command modules keep
    97	  literal `choices=` tuples (RF5), and T2 pins them and both schema enums to
    98	  the registry.
    99	- **Check 9b, `type-confused-join`** (`ilp_rewrite.check_join_types`, D12
   100	  (o), D13 (o)). A named variable's sites, including a declared comparison's
   101	  type, must have intersecting ancestor closures (`ilp.type_closures`, from
   102	  `ModelIndex.supertype_closure`). The import always passes the closures.
   103	- **SWI escapes in Popper text** (`ilp_popper`). Octal `\NNN\` (1 to 7
   104	  digits) and, after review finding 7, every form SWI 10.0.2's `writeq`
   105	  writes: `\a \b \v \f \r`, `\xN\`. Refusals are `unparsable` with a line
   106	  and column; one helper builds them all (the executed refactor).
   107	- **`extract_program`** reads Popper v5.0.1's stderr log (IL1-F4): the first
   108	  run of rules after the last solution banner, prefixes stripped (anchored
   109	  after review finding 4a).
   110	- **The Popper rendering, adapter version 3** (IL1-A1, IL1-A2):
   111	  - `bk.pl` is grouped by predicate;
   112	  - each comparison against an observed integer value is a unary threshold
   113	    predicate (`gt`, `lt`; at most 32 values per type, ranked selection),
   114	    written as ground facts over the exported values it holds for;
   115	  - thresholds that hold for no value are omitted;
   116	  - `bias.pl` lists them, with no binary comparison and no
   117	    `magic_value_type`;
   118	  - the parser maps a threshold atom back to the declared binary comparison,
   119	    so checks 5 and 9b apply unchanged.
   120	
   121	  The neutral target stays at adapter version 1.
   122	- **The evidence script** `evidence/IL1/run_popper.py`. It runs Popper under
   123	  `run_bounded_process` with all six limits, has SWI evaluate coverage
   124	  independently, imports with fixed arguments and sanitizes paths. The
   125	  install is a hash-pinned lock in a scratch prefix.
   126	
   127	**Goldens that moved, all by owner amendment:**
   128	- the X1 Popper export tree;
   129	- in `expected.json`, E for the Popper target and I2's provenance digests;
   130	- the `export_sha256` field of 19 IK5 run records.
   131	
   132	No IK5 exit code or refusal changed. No IK5 case became `type-confused-join`.
   133	The neutral target, the IK6 walk and the RF1 goldens are unchanged.
